course: dictionary
lesson: 14309
title: In a nutshell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A nutshell is the hard outer case of a nut. You can see the word nut inside it, which is a clue. «The squirrel cracked the nutshell to reach the nut inside.» The nut is inside, and the nutshell is the hard case around it.
explain: «In a nutshell» is an idiom, a group of words whose meaning is not just the meaning of each word. Do not read it word by word. Read the whole phrase and look at the words around it. «In a nutshell, plants need light, water and air.» The sentence after it tells you what is being summed up.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «In very few words, plants need light, water and air» still makes sense, so you know you have it right. Ask yourself: is the author giving the short version?
fact: A nutshell is the hard outer shell of a nut.
fact: «In a nutshell» means in very few words, said briefly.
fact: «In a nutshell» is an idiom: its meaning is not the meaning of each word.
fact: Writers and teachers use it to sum up: «In a nutshell, bees make honey from flowers.»
exercise: «The squirrel cracked the nutshell to reach the nut inside.» What is a nutshell here? | *The hard outer shell of a nut | A tiny bowl for soup | A pet's bed | A kind of soft fruit
exercise: «In a nutshell, the story is about a dog who finds his way home.» What does «in a nutshell» mean? | In a very big house | *In very few words, said briefly | Hidden inside a hard case | Very slowly, one word at a time
exercise: Mia thinks «in a nutshell» is about a real nut. What does it really mean? | Inside a hard case | *Briefly, in very few words | A very small box | Nuts are the best snack
test: «Dad said, «In a nutshell, we are moving on Saturday.»» What does Dad mean? | We are not moving at all | We are moving on Saturday, and it is a long story | We are moving to a nut farm | *We are moving on Saturday, said in very few words
test: «The walnut sat in its thick, hard nutshell.» Find and copy the word for the hard outer case of a nut. | *nutshell | sat | thick | walnut
exam: «The teacher said, «In a nutshell, bees make honey from flowers.»» What does this sentence mean? | *Bees make honey from flowers, said briefly | Bees live in very big nuts | Honey is a kind of nut | Flowers grow inside shells
